PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Majority (Colleagues 2,3,4,6,7,8,11,12) converge on C: Schedule 1 banks are federally regulated (Bank Act/Canada Labour Code), so 2021 ESA s.67.2 ban (post-Oct 2021 hires, no sale-of-business or true C-suite exception) never applies; common-law reasonableness test remains available. A/B/D/E are all provincially regulated ESA-covered roles post-ban, so clauses void. 

Minority (10,14) argue B: lawyers expressly exempt from ESA (O. Reg. 285/01), therefore statutory ban inapplicable and pre-existing common-law test governs. Counter-arguments note LSO professional-conduct rules further restrict non-competes for lawyers (Colleague 11). 

Key unresolved tension: whether ESA exemption for lawyers is functionally equivalent to federal jurisdiction for enforceability purposes. Dates of hire (all post-2021 except E) irrelevant once jurisdiction established. No support for A/D/E; E’s long tenure does not create retroactive exception.}

